1	//! Composition root for the agent harness service.
2	//!
3	//! The hexagon lives in `crates/agent_harness`; this binary is the shell around
4	//! it. Its whole job is to read the environment, turn those values into adapter
5	//! arguments, and run the Kafka consumer. It is the only place that knows both
6	//! what the config looks like and which concrete adapters are live.
7	//!
8	//! There is no HTTP server: the harness is triggered by channel messages on
9	//! `macro.channels`, not by an API call.
10	//!
11	//! Every adapter constructed here is real, but most of their *methods* are
12	//! still `todo!()`. The process starts, joins the consumer group, and logs
13	//! channel traffic; it will panic the first time a mention actually drives one
14	//! of them.
15	//!
16	//! `RuntimeAttachments` is deliberately the logging stub rather than agent_proxy:
17	//! wiring the real one means building its `PgChatRepo`, `SessionRegistry`,
18	//! `GatewayNotifier`, `PgPendingMessages`, and `RedisPostgresStreamRepo` here,
19	//! which is the next chunk of work.
20	
21	mod config;
22	
