Changes from the last version:

- `let container` / `let log`, both `Clone` with shared interior. `session.connection()` is no longer needed by this test at all.
- `ContainerMock::new(id)` — inbound is no longer seeded at construction, since `push` supersedes it. The existing test at `agent_sessions/tests.rs:20` passes an inbound array, so that call site changes too.
- `sent()` / `push()` instead of `sent_messages()` / `push_inbound()` — shorter, and the test says which direction plenty of times already.

One thing that still bugs me: `assert_sent` re-states the full history every time, so the last assertion is four lines of noise to check one new message. Options are a cursor-style `assert_eq!(container.sent_since(&mut cursor), [..])`, or just asserting the final tape once at the end and dropping the intermediate ones. I lean at keeping them — the intermediate assertions are what prove the prompt *stayed* buffered, which is the whole point of the test.

